WEBVTT

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:19.040
<b>tsukinuketa aoi sora</b>

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:19.040
<b>The blue sky has broken through</b>

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.040
<b>saa dekakeyou</b>

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.040
<b>Come, let's go out</b>

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:28.880
<b>itsumo no namikimichi jitensha wo koideku</b>

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:28.880
<b>Riding my bike through the usual avenue</b>

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:33.550
<b>ima sugu ni aitai yo</b>

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:33.550
<b>"I want to meet you now."</b>

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:37.100
<b>omoi ga kaze wo kiri</b>

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:37.100
<b>That thought is blown away by the wind,</b>

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:44.770
<b>kimi e to hakondeku tegami ni natte</b>

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:44.770
<b>and becomes a letter being carried to you</b>

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:52.360
<b>koko kara hajimaru monogatari fly!</b>

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:52.360
<b>The story that starts from here... Fly!</b>

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:59.620
<b>kawariyuku kisetsu ga ashioto wo tatetemo</b>

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:59.620
<b>Even if the changing seasons walk on with loud footsteps,</b>

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:06.500
<b>sou kawaranai suki to iu tsubasa</b>

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:06.500
<b>the wings of love won't change</b>

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:14.510
<b>dokomade mo tondeke oozora takaku</b>

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:14.510
<b>Fly far away, high into the sky</b>

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:20.680
<b>koi no tenki yohou hare nochi hare ni nare</b>

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:20.680
<b>May the weather forecast of love be sunny and clear forever</b>

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:28.350
<b>ashita mo asatte mo</b>

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:28.350
<b>Tomorrow and the day after tomorrow</b>

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:37.950
Welcome 
to Izumo, 
land of 
legend

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:41.490
<b>Episode 12     The Mysterious Adventure</b>

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.910
For one month starting today,

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:44.870
she will study together with us.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:48.080
Hitotsubashi Yurie-sama.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:53.670
I'm sure you are already aware, 
but Hitotsubashi-sama is a god.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.380
Be sure to mind your manners.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:57.180
Yes.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.930
Er, there's no need for such formality—

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:03.310
Don't be silly!

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:06.180
You are still a god, middle schooler or not.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:08.900
Izumo is a land that honors the gods.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:18.030
Please take your seat.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:46.470
A business trip?

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:47.640
Yes.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:50.690
You know October is the godless month, right?

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:51.810
Note: According to legend, the gods from all over Japan gather at Izumo Shrine in October. Because they are absent from their locations during that time, October has been called kannazuki, "godless month".

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:51.810
Yes.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:57.780
Gods from all over Japan gather in 
Izumo for a month and have a meeting.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.070
Please attend this meeting as well.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:09.330
Do I have to go to Izumo every day?

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.590
If possible, it would be more 
efficient to move there for a month.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.170
Move there?

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:19.260
My mom and dad would never allow that!

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.300
But this is a very important event.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:27.100
I'll try convincing your parents as well.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:33.350
Lodging and meals will be 
arranged for by the association.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.730
But I'll be gone for a month—

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:53.080
What we learned so far will come up during 
the midterm exam, so be sure to review it well.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:54.290
Rise!

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:57.750
Bow!

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.140
They're much further ahead than our school—

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:09.100
Hitotsubashi-sama.

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.850
I am the class representative, Abe Naoto.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:14.480
Hello.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:17.770
I will be the one to take care of you.

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:21.110
Thank you.

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:24.160
If something is bothering you, 
do not hesitate to tell me.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:25.740
Er—

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:28.430
I'm a transfer student.

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:29.920
A classmate.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:33.250
Can't we talk a little more casually?

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:39.460
But we decided at the class meeting not 
to be rude to you, since you are god.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:44.550
It's true that I'm a god, but I'm a student before that.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:48.430
I'd rather you call me "Hitotsubashi" or "Yurie".

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:52.160
Understood.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:54.310
I will bring it up during the next class meeting.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:04.280
Excuse me, where can I find the school shop?

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:08.530
Yes, it's beside the stairs on the first floor.

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:10.730
I see.

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:11.700
Thanks.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:16.540
Umm—

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.090
She left.

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:28.090
Ma'am, two pork cutlet sandwiches!

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:29.850
A fried soba bread roll!

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:31.060
And a cream roll!

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:34.600
Hey, don't cut in line!

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:36.390
It's incredibly crowded—

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:38.220
Excuse me!

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:40.730
A sandwich please!

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:43.690
Here you go! A fried soba roll and a cream roll!

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:44.190
Thank you!

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:46.780
Any bread is fine!

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:48.410
Hey, watch it!

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:49.820
I-I'm sorry—

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:52.030
Hitotsubashi-sama!

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:05.130
Please.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:08.090
I— Er—

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:27.780
Everyone is so cold—

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:31.070
They're all too formal—

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:33.870
Everyone is minding their manners.

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:37.790
They only know you as the god Yurie-sama here.

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:42.290
But I have to ask them about the midterm exam.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:48.300
Well, let's leave this matter for now.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:52.760
Yurie-sama, could you wait at the front gate after class?

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.810
Someone will come and pick you up.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:57.100
I don't mind.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.520
And then Itaru-chan from math class—

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:01.940
Yeah I know, he was in trouble!

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:06.320
Excuse us.

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:07.690
Sorry for bothering you.

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:10.820
Umm, I don't mind—

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:15.080
I don't mind at all.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.910
They're frightened of you.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:21.370
"Let sleeping gods lie and they won't curse you," huh?

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:25.340
I won't curse them—

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:41.890
One month sure is long.

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:45.730
Our shrine will definitely go in the red now.

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:48.070
It'll just go back to how it used to be.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:53.660
Just do normal business like an honest shrine.

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:56.620
I can't live like that anymore.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.920
I wonder if Yurie is doing well?

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:04.800
She'll be fine.

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:06.710
She's not a little kid anymore.

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:09.630
Where's Hitotsubashi-san?

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:11.920
Is she sick today?

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:14.380
Didn't you hear yesterday?

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:16.520
She transferred to Izumo.

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:17.810
Why?

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:20.390
She has to attend a meeting of the gods there.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:25.350
When will she return?

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:28.360
I heard she'd return next month—

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:30.230
Oh, I see—

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:31.390
Why?

00:08:31.390 --> 00:08:33.070
Do you have some business with her?

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:37.200
No, it's not like that, but—

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:42.040
It just feels like something is missing if she isn't here.

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:47.460
Did you hear that just now!?

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:52.420
Do you think he's interested in Yurie?

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:55.380
He's at least aware of her existence!

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:57.180
Oh my!

00:08:57.850 --> 00:09:01.060
Yurie would be overjoyed if she knew—

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:10.020
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:14.280
I'm sorry, you must've been waiting for me.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:15.570
Not at all. Let's go.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:21.990
Hitotsubashi-sama!

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:24.120
Wanna try inviting her?

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:25.210
Sure.

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:29.290
Yurie-sama!

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:34.720
What's that!?

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:37.300
We've come to pick you up!

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:39.260
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:40.970
Better yet, we're sorry to keep yo—

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:43.310
Please, get on.

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:48.100
We're gonna ride all the way to the Kami-sama 
Convention grounds, or "Kamicon" for short!

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.480
But, well—

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:52.600
It's all right.

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:54.990
Other people can't see us.

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:56.950
Of course, those two can't either.

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:08.370
Who— was she talking to just now?

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:09.080
Beats me.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:10.580
See you later.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:26.140
So she really was a god.

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:16.230
Last stop, the Kamicon meeting grounds!

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:28.580
Well then, we will come back for you tomorrow morning.

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:29.290
Okay.

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:30.160
Thanks.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:31.960
Please enjoy yourself.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:33.960
Don't get lost.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:00.950
Where should I go?

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:03.820
Hey, it's the newcomer from a while back.

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:06.030
Mr. President?

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:09.240
Out of thousands of gods, you 
are the last one to arrive again?

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:10.830
Your head must be in the clouds.

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:13.550
I'm sorry.

00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:15.080
I had school.

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:16.300
It's no biggie.

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:21.130
In a crowd like this, no one's going to 
notice one or two people coming in late.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:26.510
Err, so, what exactly should I be doing here?

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:28.510
Today's the opening day.

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:32.230
You can start by gathering some 
knowledge at an introductory course.

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:40.320
I see, so you are already retired?

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:41.490
What a shame.

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:44.450
I always enjoyed the depressions you created.

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:47.530
It's not like I'm completely retired yet—

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:50.410
I guess you could say I'm just inactive at the moment.

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:52.370
Oh, I see.

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:53.520
See you later.

00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:55.830
Once you're in the mood again, let me know.

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:03.220
The god of death is cheerful as ever.

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:09.710
Oh?

00:13:09.710 --> 00:13:11.180
Poverty god?

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:13.900
Y-Yashima-sama!

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:15.350
What are you doing?

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:18.800
Benten-sama is holding a live performance,

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:20.480
so I bought some cheering goods—

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:27.570
Is Yurie-sama here already?

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:31.290
Team Happiness should have picked her up.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:34.250
I guess she's doing introductory courses then?

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:39.880
Participate in as many programs as 
possible, and improve your divine powers.

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:42.840
You will receive a stamp for 
every course you participate in.

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:47.090
If you collect 20 stamps, you will 
receive a special gift on the final day.

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:51.060
That is all.

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:56.060
Yurie-sama!

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:06.030
There are so many, I don't know which ones I should go to—

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:10.490
Why not start with the ones that interest you?

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:12.120
That interest me?

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:12.910
Yes.

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:15.770
I think you should try to find something

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:19.460
that could help you decide what kind 
of god you want to become in the future.

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:23.920
What kind of god?

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:33.350
Well, I have some business to attend to, so—

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:41.690
He's a groupie, I tell you.

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:52.370
I'll take a rest and think about it.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:56.790
Good evening, everyone!

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:59.250
Good evening!

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:02.140
Let's start with the first song.

00:15:02.140 --> 00:15:03.210
Please enjoy.

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:23.060
A god can't afford to be late!

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:32.820
<i>I envy the gods that don't have school—</i>

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:38.580
Hitotsubashi-sama.

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:41.090
Yes?

00:15:41.090 --> 00:15:44.130
We had a discussion at the class meeting—

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:48.840
The class decided to call 
you Yurie-sama from now on.

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:56.260
The most preferred names were Yurie-sama, 
Hitotsubashi-sama and Hitotsubashi-san respectively.

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:56.260
Yurie-sama

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:56.260
Hitotsubashi-sama

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:56.260
Hitotsubashi-san

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:56.260
Kami-sama

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:56.260
Yurie-chan

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:56.260
Votes

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:58.700
Is it okay if we call you Yurie-sama?

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:01.740
I guess it's okay.

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:04.690
But it's still a little stiff.

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:10.010
You dropped this.

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:17.490
Thanks—

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:18.700
You're welcome—

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:25.210
Kondou Isami, Serizawa Kamo and the others 
that remained in Kyoto formed the Shinsengumi.

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:30.010
This happened after shogun 
Iemochi's return to the capital,

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:33.300
with the remaining Roushitai members 
from Edo that were ordered to protect him.

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:35.550
They were then called the Shinchougumi.

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:39.220
Under the command of the Military Commissioner of Kyoto

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:36.600
Yurie-sama!

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:39.220
Yurie-sama!

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:41.600
and Aizu domain, the Shinsengumi stayed in the city—

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:42.770
Hey!

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:49.980
Don't pass around weird notes during class!

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:25.100
Fortune strips in the 
21st century: What will 
become of them? 
Hitotsubashi Yurie

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:23.730
Petit luck

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:25.100
Great luck
(highest)

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:25.100
Ultra great luck

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:23.850
Petit luck

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:24.230
Petit luck

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:24.350
Petit luck

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:24.480
Petit luck

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:24.600
Petit luck

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:25.100
Petit luck

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:26.520
<b>Attendance card</b>

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:34.950
<b>Midterm examination</b>

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:08.690
<b>Kamichu</b>

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:18.570
<b>Midterm examination result</b>

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:23.490
<b>Hitotsubashi Yurie-sama</b>

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:22.950
She must've been busy.

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:23.490
Yeah.

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:30.080
Yurie-sama?

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:42.850
They were much further ahead—

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:45.720
And I haven't had much time to study—

00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:50.310
The textbooks were different—

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:53.690
And I couldn't ask anyone for help!

00:18:57.190 --> 00:18:58.450
I want to go home!

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:08.830
Cheer up.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:10.540
Who cares about grades?

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:13.250
They are of no importance to a god.

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:16.920
They're very important to middle schoolers.

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:22.010
I wonder where Yashima-sama is?

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:25.060
I'm gonna go look for him for a bit.

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:39.650
Okay, I'll wait outside.

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:44.870
Hey, is this seat taken?

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:46.950
Go ahead.

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:53.710
Are you the god of death?

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:56.670
I-I'm not!

00:19:56.670 --> 00:19:58.380
Oh really?

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:00.510
You were looking so gloomy.

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:06.010
Gods should be cheerful all the time.

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:08.640
For the sake of the people who believe in you.

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:12.230
I'm a middle school student.

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:14.600
But you're here, aren't you?

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:16.900
That means you're a god.

00:20:18.530 --> 00:20:21.860
Can't gods have problems?

00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:23.570
Sure they can.

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:28.830
However, we can't ask god for help.

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:36.210
In the end, the only things 
you can rely on are yourself—

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:39.800
and your friends.

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:45.640
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.430
Sorry for the wait!

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:53.270
See ya.

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:02.530
Friends?

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:07.490
B-Benten-sama!?

00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:04.300
A month passes by so quickly.

00:22:04.300 --> 00:22:07.380
Yurie-sama will go home today.

00:22:08.840 --> 00:22:12.430
Things may have been unpleasant 
for you here, but Yurie-sama—

00:22:13.350 --> 00:22:18.100
Could you perhaps give us all some final blessings?

00:22:27.280 --> 00:22:28.660
I'm sorry!

00:22:31.030 --> 00:22:34.240
I got the chance to meet all of you—

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:35.880
I—

00:22:36.600 --> 00:22:37.870
Was a coward.

00:22:38.620 --> 00:22:43.250
I think I should have taken more initiative 
to approach and talk to everyone.

00:22:44.920 --> 00:22:50.800
I'm shy and get nervous fast, 
so I quickly lose my composure.

00:22:51.220 --> 00:22:55.770
But that's the same for everyone, so that's no excuse—

00:22:57.100 --> 00:23:05.280
I should have become friends with everyone as 
middle school god Hitotsubashi Yurie from the start!

00:23:05.280 --> 00:23:07.650
So, I'm sorry!

00:23:13.580 --> 00:23:15.200
Hitotsubashi-sama?

00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:17.290
Me too!

00:23:21.580 --> 00:23:26.050
I wanted to become friends with you too!

00:23:28.010 --> 00:23:29.260
Me too!

00:23:29.260 --> 00:23:30.260
Me too!

00:23:30.260 --> 00:23:30.970
Me too!

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:35.310
Yurie-sama!

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:36.720
Yes?

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:40.230
Please attend this school again next year.

00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:45.650
When that time comes, I want 
to welcome you as "Yurie-chan".

00:23:47.780 --> 00:23:52.410
Err, could you take a vote on that in a class meeting?

00:23:52.410 --> 00:23:54.030
We don't need to vote on that.

00:23:54.030 --> 00:23:55.370
Everyone agrees with it!

00:23:55.780 --> 00:23:57.080
Please come again next year!

00:23:57.080 --> 00:23:58.330
I'm looking forward to it!

00:23:58.330 --> 00:23:59.150
Yurie-chan!

00:23:59.150 --> 00:24:00.330
See you next year!

00:24:29.150 --> 00:24:30.280
Welcome home.

00:24:30.820 --> 00:24:33.570
Looks like you were able to get back by yourself.

00:24:34.410 --> 00:24:35.570
Mitsue-chan!

00:24:36.370 --> 00:24:37.620
Matsuri-chan!

00:24:43.750 --> 00:24:45.250
I missed you!

00:24:46.000 --> 00:24:47.760
Same here.

00:24:47.760 --> 00:24:50.380
You must've been lonely all by yourself.

00:24:51.090 --> 00:24:53.510
Nope, not at all.

00:24:54.470 --> 00:24:55.720
Not at all.

00:24:57.140 --> 00:24:58.100
Really?

00:25:00.100 --> 00:25:02.930
I made a lot of friends!

00:25:07.110 --> 00:25:13.190
<b>mada mada zenzen owannai last ichijikan no jugyou desu</b>

00:25:07.110 --> 00:25:13.190
<b>The last class of the day never seems to end</b>

00:25:13.190 --> 00:25:18.070
<b>tokei wo chira chira mitemo ichi byou ga nagai ne</b>

00:25:13.190 --> 00:25:18.070
<b>Even if I keep glancing at my watch, a second seems an eternity</b>

00:25:19.080 --> 00:25:25.120
<b>mabushii koutei mieru kimi no hashiru sugata oikake</b>

00:25:19.080 --> 00:25:25.120
<b>In the radiant schoolyard, trailing your running visage,</b>

00:25:25.120 --> 00:25:30.250
<b>houkago love-love date mousou shite bosou chuu</b>

00:25:25.120 --> 00:25:30.250
<b>my imagination is running wild about our date after class</b>

00:25:31.170 --> 00:25:34.170
<b>chime no kane koi no signal</b>

00:25:31.170 --> 00:25:34.170
<b>The school chimes ring and it's a signal of love!</b>

00:25:34.170 --> 00:25:37.180
<b>rouka no tobidashi ni wa chuui</b>

00:25:34.170 --> 00:25:37.180
<b>Be careful if you rush out into the hallway!</b>

00:25:37.180 --> 00:25:40.140
<b>kimi no moto e ichiban saki ni</b>

00:25:37.180 --> 00:25:40.140
<b>I dash to see you, first thing!</b>

00:25:40.140 --> 00:25:42.770
<b>issho ni kaerou</b>

00:25:40.140 --> 00:25:42.770
<b>Let's go home together!</b>

00:25:43.730 --> 00:25:50.400
<b>soda aji no ice candy gira gira na ohisama no shita hanbunko</b>

00:25:43.730 --> 00:25:50.400
<b>Sharing a soda-flavored popsicle under the glaring sun</b>

00:25:50.400 --> 00:25:56.450
<b>torokesou na atashi no seishun desu doki doki shichau</b>

00:25:50.400 --> 00:25:56.450
<b>My youth seems to melt with it, it makes my heart beat faster</b>

00:25:56.450 --> 00:26:01.910
<b>kono nanigenai toki wo ima mune ni shimatte</b>

00:25:56.450 --> 00:26:01.910
<b>I'm shutting our casual time in my heart</b>

00:26:02.200 --> 00:26:09.330
<b>asu wa mata kyou yori mo kimi wo suki ni naru no desu</b>

00:26:02.200 --> 00:26:09.330
<b>Tomorrow I will love you even more than today</b>

00:26:13.520 --> 00:26:31.540
<b>Preview</b>

00:26:14.340 --> 00:26:17.010
Even gods celebrate Christmas.

00:26:17.010 --> 00:26:22.830
But this year Matsuri-chan is planning an event by and for the Shinto shrine.

00:26:22.830 --> 00:26:24.020
How exciting!

00:26:24.600 --> 00:26:26.440
Next episode, "Do What You Want".

00:26:26.440 --> 00:26:28.850
A Merry Christmas to chu!

00:26:26.480 --> 00:26:31.540
<b>Do What You Want</b>
